WEBVTT

00:00:02.120 --> 00:00:03.540
Sanada-san, can you hear me?

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:04.920
Sanada-san?

00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:07.790
Yes. This is Sanada from the scene.

00:00:07.790 --> 00:00:11.510
The UN Inquiry Group has just entered.

00:00:11.510 --> 00:00:20.060
Our sources tell us that the purpose of this investigation by the Japanese goverment is to negate the rumor that a strategic nuke was used.

00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.880
A lot of people died, huh?

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:26.440
If only I had done as Birdy instructed...

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:34.000
It wasn't wrong of you to want to save Nakasugi-san.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:35.970
That may be, but...

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:41.120
And those most at fault were the ones who brought the Ryunka to Earth.

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:48.210
The Federation thought it was okay to sacrifice the people of Earth in order to annihilate the Ryunka too.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:50.760
I'm sorry, Tsutomu.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:53.770
You didn't do anything wrong.

00:00:54.450 --> 00:00:57.460
Also, you're lending me your body again.

00:00:58.310 --> 00:01:01.970
Um... It's okay if you turn into Birdy when you want to.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.310
After all, this time I said, "Please kill me."

00:01:07.310 --> 00:01:09.310
I'm so happy!

00:01:10.100 --> 00:01:11.640
Thanks, Tsutomu.

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:13.960
Make sure you change your clothing and hair color to something normal.

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:15.820
I know, I know!

00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:19.120
I brought Shion's clothes with me, so I'll be fine.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:20.620
Now, to get changed!

00:01:38.410 --> 00:01:41.090
You're an Altarian, aren't you?

00:01:41.090 --> 00:01:42.420
You...

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:48.470
I was walking around to see if there were any Altarians wandering the streets.

00:01:48.470 --> 00:01:50.470
The Altarian Network, huh?

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:55.480
You don't look like just a refugee.

00:01:55.800 --> 00:01:58.110
You're connected to that mysterious light incident, aren't you?

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:02.820
Either way, you're some sort of military special forces person, right?

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.780
You experimented with some weird weapon on Earth, didn't you?

00:02:06.760 --> 00:02:08.020
I...

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.740
Well, you're probably a sacrificial pawn, though.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:15.580
Word on the street says that even shook the Justice Board, so if you returned to the Federation, you'd be living in a jail cell.

00:02:17.540 --> 00:02:18.250
I...

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:21.630
How about you stay here?

00:02:24.810 --> 00:02:26.390
This is Arita Shion.

00:02:30.010 --> 00:02:32.070
Tokyo is no good for the time being.

00:02:32.070 --> 00:02:35.940
But, we must eat!

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:39.230
Thus, if Tokyo is no good, then Kansai!

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:40.020
Kansai.

00:02:40.020 --> 00:02:43.960
Moreover, in Kobe, we'll open an outdoor live!

00:02:43.960 --> 00:02:46.200
So, why Arita Shion?

00:02:46.760 --> 00:02:48.630
There are rumors of terrorism.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:51.870
These days, the big players probably won't take on live shows.

00:02:51.870 --> 00:02:53.430
Thus, we go with the cult!

00:02:55.390 --> 00:03:01.110
This way, if by some fluke, Arita Shion becomes big, our company will survive.

00:03:05.860 --> 00:03:09.600
But why that gravure idol again?

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:23.360
No! I have no intention of opposing the Justice Board's intentions.

00:03:23.690 --> 00:03:26.570
I heard that you got a day off.

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:29.490
You sure found out quickly.

00:03:29.510 --> 00:03:32.160
I'm not the boss just for show.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:35.750
For the next little while, you'll earn your living as Arita Shion.

00:03:35.750 --> 00:03:37.170
No way.

00:03:37.990 --> 00:03:40.500
What do you intend to do about this place's rent?

00:03:40.500 --> 00:03:42.300
Do you even <i>have</i> an allowance?

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:45.260
Can you live on without your beloved onigiri?

00:03:45.260 --> 00:03:47.330
I-I see.

00:03:47.330 --> 00:03:50.250
Money is needed to live on Earth...

00:03:50.250 --> 00:03:51.870
Hey, do you have any money?

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:53.350
My allowance barely cuts it.

00:03:53.350 --> 00:03:53.720
Your tea is ready.
My allowance barely cuts it.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:55.140
Figures.
Your tea is ready.

00:03:56.730 --> 00:03:59.020
B-Birdy the Berserker Killer?

00:03:59.290 --> 00:04:02.440
This girl is our talent, Arita Shion.

00:04:03.910 --> 00:04:04.900
A newbie?

00:04:06.160 --> 00:04:10.200
I'm Cappela, nice to meet you.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:14.290
I'll have her working as your manager and assistant.

00:04:16.250 --> 00:04:17.730
Hers?!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.750
Nice to meet you, Cappela-chan.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.500
That, I am!

00:04:21.500 --> 00:04:23.920
I'm a high school student!

00:04:24.270 --> 00:04:25.300
Shion-chan!

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:27.670
Meow!

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:29.840
That's great! That's great!

00:04:31.040 --> 00:04:34.210
It's the first work we've done in a while, but you're as great as ever, Shion-chan.

00:04:34.210 --> 00:04:36.030
Thank you.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:38.520
Next week is your charity live, right?

00:04:38.520 --> 00:04:40.650
B-Bicycle club?

00:04:40.650 --> 00:04:42.070
There you go again.

00:04:42.070 --> 00:04:43.920
This, Shion-chan.

00:04:45.310 --> 00:04:48.650
I'll be coming to see you too, so do your best, Shiorin.

00:04:48.650 --> 00:04:52.030
I'll do my best.

00:04:52.030 --> 00:04:54.510
Ah, you haven't heard yet?

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.040
Not a word!

00:04:56.040 --> 00:04:58.650
Anyway, it's next weekend starting Friday.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:02.250
It's at Kobe, so make sure you're not late.

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:04.410
Wh— Hello?

00:05:04.410 --> 00:05:04.680
W-Wait...

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:08.720
The meeting time is 6:30 AM at Tokyo Station.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:13.100
Kobe, huh?

00:05:13.680 --> 00:05:15.330
Have you been there before?

00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:17.230
No, I haven't, but...

00:05:18.350 --> 00:05:20.330
Nakasugi-san is there.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.680
Are you well, Hayamiya?

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:25.980
I'm doing well.

00:05:26.760 --> 00:05:31.460
The week since I arrived has passed just like that.

00:05:31.460 --> 00:05:35.300
Being in an all girls high school has sort of a strange feeling to it,

00:05:35.300 --> 00:05:37.200
but as I get used to it, it has its interesting parts.

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:40.510
I wonder if she really is doing well.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.260
I've somehow gotten used to life on the farm, too.

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:00.640
Yes?

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.400
Good grief. You're still dressed like that?

00:06:03.750 --> 00:06:06.360
Didn't you promise to look after the cows this morning?

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:07.840
I'm sorry.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.530
I wasn't feeling well.

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.660
I won't listen to such selfishness.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:14.750
Hurry up and change and head to the barn.

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:21.790
What are you doing?

00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:26.460
Even the cow-handling of Tokyo-raised ladies is ladylike, huh?

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:31.080
Go on now. If you don't hurry, you'll be late.

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:38.270
Even if it is <i>our</i> Reporting Society, we cannot ignore this incident!

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:39.820
You mean <i>you</i> can't, right?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:42.700
We don't have any way of getting information about it.

00:06:42.700 --> 00:06:44.810
Even the U.N. is here investigating, after all.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:48.200
The specifics of the cause have yet to be determined!

00:06:48.200 --> 00:06:50.820
On the net, they're even saying stuff like "a chemical weapon was used."

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:53.570
Stop believing rumors like that!

00:06:53.570 --> 00:06:57.060
And yet they say smoke does not rise where there is no fire!

00:06:57.060 --> 00:07:00.540
Raising smoke where there is no fire is what a rumor does!

00:07:00.540 --> 00:07:06.950
Isn't it the duty of journalists to accurately report information to the people so they are not misled by rumors?

00:07:06.950 --> 00:07:09.140
As expected! Well spoken, Hayamiya.

00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:12.270
Senkawa!

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:17.280
We're going to Shinagawa next weekend.

00:07:17.280 --> 00:07:18.760
We have to see, even if it's from far away.

00:07:18.760 --> 00:07:20.380
Weekend...

00:07:20.380 --> 00:07:23.540
Ah, no, I can't. I have something I need to do...

00:07:23.540 --> 00:07:25.550
What? Us, too!

00:07:25.550 --> 00:07:29.150
There's Shiorin's concert in Kobe!

00:07:29.150 --> 00:07:31.230
Shiorin is so moe, isn't she?

00:07:34.480 --> 00:07:36.570
Could it be... You are also—

00:07:36.570 --> 00:07:39.800
Eh? Oh, no. I'm going to help my relatives.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:40.580
Where?

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:43.290
Kobe.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:44.200
Kobe!

00:07:44.200 --> 00:07:48.110
You <i>are</i> going to see Shiorin's concert, like I thought, Senkawa!

00:07:48.110 --> 00:07:49.620
Senkawa!

00:07:49.620 --> 00:07:51.430
You can't tell me I'm wrong!

00:07:51.430 --> 00:07:52.670
Kobe...
You can't tell me I'm wrong!

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:55.820
Senkawa!

00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:58.690
You're going to Kobe, right?

00:07:58.690 --> 00:07:59.860
Uh, yeah.

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:01.250
Here, then.

00:08:07.940 --> 00:08:10.650
Nakasugi-san's new address, huh?

00:08:10.650 --> 00:08:11.820
Want to go see her later?

00:08:13.150 --> 00:08:15.280
What's wrong? Aren't you going to eat?

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:20.450
Of course! I've been looking forward to this.

00:08:22.020 --> 00:08:23.660
It's delicious!

00:08:27.040 --> 00:08:30.180
The guidebook said there's a Chinatown, didn't it?

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:32.000
Didn't you just eat a lunchbox?

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:34.590
I want to try lots of Earth foods.

00:08:34.590 --> 00:08:36.340
I received my allowance, too.

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.590
What are you doing?

00:08:38.900 --> 00:08:40.400
Come on already.

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.740
Coming!

00:08:44.150 --> 00:08:45.720
Ah, here it is.

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:46.350
This is the inn.

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:49.690
It kind of feels like this inn alone is from a different era.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:52.920
It's midday and yet it's pitch dark in here.

00:08:52.920 --> 00:08:55.150
All three of us in here?

00:08:55.150 --> 00:08:58.070
We're only here for two or three days, so it'll be plenty.

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:01.580
Um, do we have free time?

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:03.810
It's not like we came here for fun.

00:09:03.810 --> 00:09:04.530
I know.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:08.870
Well, make sure you're back in time for dinner.

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:12.230
Thank you!

00:09:21.020 --> 00:09:22.780
Wow, you can see a long way.

00:09:22.780 --> 00:09:25.160
You're completely in the tourist mood, aren't you?

00:09:25.160 --> 00:09:27.320
You have a meeting at night, don't you?

00:09:28.050 --> 00:09:29.350
Let's look over there.

00:09:30.930 --> 00:09:32.840
You know...

00:09:39.950 --> 00:09:42.410
Huh? Hey, isn't this—

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:49.990
You're a coward, so I came for you.

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:51.810
Cut that out, would you?

00:09:52.340 --> 00:09:55.550
You want to make sure Nakasugi is safe, don't you?

00:09:55.550 --> 00:09:57.250
Yeah, but...

00:10:06.520 --> 00:10:12.020
Sayaka-san, if you don't hurry and go clean the sheepfold, the sheep will return before you're done.

00:10:12.020 --> 00:10:12.980
Yes.

00:10:15.780 --> 00:10:18.700
Nakasugi-san did say they were distant relatives...

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:20.110
Like I thought...

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:22.820
Hey, Birdy!

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:25.320
Hello!

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:34.370
If you want ice cream, it's at that stand over there.

00:10:34.370 --> 00:10:37.850
Ah, no. More importantly, that looks heavy.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:38.710
Want some help?

00:10:42.080 --> 00:10:44.590
Ah, I'm fairly athletic.

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.810
Are you from Tokyo by any chance?

00:10:49.220 --> 00:10:53.260
They're so soft and fluffy, like stuffed toys.

00:10:54.700 --> 00:10:57.640
Are you here in Kobe alone, Miss?

00:10:57.640 --> 00:10:59.730
Ah, yeah, I guess.

00:11:03.660 --> 00:11:05.620
It's such a pretty place, isn't it?

00:11:05.620 --> 00:11:09.030
This is my favorite spot.

00:11:09.340 --> 00:11:10.720
Really?

00:11:14.880 --> 00:11:16.220
Miss...

00:11:16.940 --> 00:11:20.010
You'll be returning to Tokyo soon, won't you?

00:11:21.390 --> 00:11:22.460
Yeah.

00:11:22.780 --> 00:11:24.700
After just meeting...

00:11:24.700 --> 00:11:26.430
We are soon to part, aren't we?

00:11:30.010 --> 00:11:31.450
Ah, I'm sorry.

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:34.180
It's rude of me to speak like that.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:41.070
Can I come play again tomorrow?

00:11:42.770 --> 00:11:44.780
Well, see you again tomorrow!

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:55.500
At least the bath is big and comfy!

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:58.080
Hey, Birdy, are you really going to go tomorrow?

00:11:58.080 --> 00:12:00.480
You mean you're okay seeing her like that?

00:12:00.480 --> 00:12:04.710
You want to cheer up Nakasugi-san somehow.

00:12:05.110 --> 00:12:06.820
You help, too.

00:12:06.820 --> 00:12:10.140
Huh? What do you mean by "help?"

00:12:12.010 --> 00:12:14.970
The lady from Tokyo is putting on airs, eh?

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:19.300
It looks like she comes here after she takes care of the cows and sheep in the barn.

00:12:19.300 --> 00:12:23.150
Whoa, what a hard job for a lady, huh?

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.110
Hayamiya?

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.590
Yep, I'm doing well.

00:12:44.150 --> 00:12:45.630
Yep, I'm fine.

00:12:46.000 --> 00:12:47.550
I've made friends, too.

00:12:51.030 --> 00:12:53.300
It kind of seems like she's overdoing it.

00:12:53.860 --> 00:12:57.060
The truth is, Nakasugi-san is lonely.

00:13:14.970 --> 00:13:16.370
That's a good dog, isn't it?

00:13:17.290 --> 00:13:18.540
Shion-san.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:21.430
I didn't think you'd really come.

00:13:21.430 --> 00:13:23.000
I had some spare time anyways.

00:13:23.890 --> 00:13:25.590
It's somewhat strange.

00:13:25.590 --> 00:13:26.420
What is?

00:13:26.740 --> 00:13:30.870
Everyone should be disappearing from my life, and yet...

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:36.530
The people I loved...

00:13:36.530 --> 00:13:38.190
They all disappeared.

00:13:39.680 --> 00:13:43.390
When I was young, my parents died in an accident.

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:47.560
When that happened, I was so sad...

00:13:48.160 --> 00:13:49.510
And lonely...

00:13:50.610 --> 00:13:54.640
But before I knew it, I forgot even those feelings,

00:13:55.270 --> 00:13:59.750
and thought of my mother and father being gone as normal.

00:14:03.350 --> 00:14:08.310
Just recently, my beloved grandfather died, too.

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:12.720
But... But...

00:14:13.700 --> 00:14:16.130
I'm sure one day, I'll forget that, too.

00:14:16.960 --> 00:14:18.470
I'm afraid of becoming like that.

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:20.890
Nakasugi-san...

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:25.380
So now... Being alone is better!

00:14:25.380 --> 00:14:27.580
I don't want to start loving anyone!

00:14:28.240 --> 00:14:29.340
I know what you mean.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:32.780
A long time ago...

00:14:33.610 --> 00:14:36.350
Someone very important to me died, too.

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:40.720
When that happened, I was so lonely and frustrated...

00:14:40.720 --> 00:14:42.340
I couldn't forgive myself.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:47.920
But there was someone there for me then.

00:14:51.610 --> 00:14:52.840
Shion-san.

00:14:54.560 --> 00:14:57.860
I'm sure there is someone there for you too.

00:14:58.620 --> 00:14:59.950
People, you see...

00:14:59.950 --> 00:15:05.140
I believe meeting many different people is the most important and happy thing there is.

00:15:05.940 --> 00:15:10.950
Even if you part, somewhere, you will certainly...

00:15:11.570 --> 00:15:12.860
Somewhere...

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:30.670
Baron...

00:15:31.550 --> 00:15:34.110
Nakasugi-san, stay close.

00:15:41.450 --> 00:15:42.870
What's wrong?

00:15:42.870 --> 00:15:43.890
That's...

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:57.740
Shion-san!

00:16:02.970 --> 00:16:03.660
That's...

00:16:03.660 --> 00:16:05.260
Birdy! Nakasugi-san is—

00:16:19.720 --> 00:16:21.730
That's a Rauna Model 1.

00:16:21.730 --> 00:16:22.760
Eh? Isn't that—

00:16:22.760 --> 00:16:24.260
It came from the Federation.

00:16:24.260 --> 00:16:25.680
Why?

00:16:25.680 --> 00:16:28.050
We'll know that when we catch it!

00:16:42.550 --> 00:16:45.330
I'd love to eat some Kobe beef steak, Bro!

00:16:45.640 --> 00:16:49.080
Hell yeah, we'll eat 'till we can't eat anymore.

00:16:52.460 --> 00:16:53.920
Ouch!

00:16:53.920 --> 00:16:55.600
Shit!

00:16:55.600 --> 00:16:56.710
Why?!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:14.730
Hand that girl over.

00:17:15.340 --> 00:17:17.370
Don't come any closer.

00:17:17.370 --> 00:17:19.700
If you come any closer, I will kill this human.

00:17:24.740 --> 00:17:27.200
This isn't good. It called down a spaceship.

00:17:27.960 --> 00:17:29.310
Birdy!

00:17:29.310 --> 00:17:32.150
Tsutomu-kun, you want to save Nakasugi-san, right?

00:17:32.150 --> 00:17:33.900
Of course I do!

00:17:33.900 --> 00:17:35.800
Then work with me.

00:17:37.560 --> 00:17:38.640
It's a camouflage.

00:17:38.640 --> 00:17:40.470
Run towards the marionette like that! Charge!

00:17:40.470 --> 00:17:41.920
Wait, what?!

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:05.870
Violin.

00:18:30.190 --> 00:18:31.140
Tsutomu.

00:18:31.140 --> 00:18:32.060
Birdy!

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:49.870
Nejula.

00:18:50.360 --> 00:18:51.720
Why are you—

00:18:53.360 --> 00:18:56.260
I don't believe I have any obligation to explain myself to you. However...

00:19:00.180 --> 00:19:04.340
In any case, considering that I saved you, is it not reasonable to thank me?

00:19:05.950 --> 00:19:07.140
Thank you.

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:09.980
Those words were quite filled with emotion.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.020
I'm moved.

00:19:11.330 --> 00:19:15.770
But why was Nakasugi-san targeted by a marionette?

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:18.580
She was the Ryunka's host.

00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:20.270
Is that not enough?

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.190
Stop acting all superior and tell me!

00:19:22.190 --> 00:19:26.480
There is the possibility that microscopic fragments of the Ryunka remain in the host.

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:27.920
No way!

00:19:27.920 --> 00:19:32.010
We also believe that the possibility is negligible.

00:19:32.010 --> 00:19:35.860
But there were those in the Federation who bet on that possibility,

00:19:35.860 --> 00:19:38.260
and sent this thing to Earth.

00:19:38.260 --> 00:19:40.290
Who was it who did it?

00:19:40.550 --> 00:19:43.050
I'll know once I investigate this marionette.

00:19:53.120 --> 00:19:55.220
That ship is also under my control now.

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:58.600
Those who schemed up the Ryunka plan won't be able to run any longer.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:01.370
You used me as bait, didn't you?

00:20:01.370 --> 00:20:03.130
You just realized?

00:20:03.130 --> 00:20:04.150
You!

00:20:04.720 --> 00:20:06.320
I appreciate your cooperation.

00:20:10.340 --> 00:20:11.830
That woman...

00:20:11.830 --> 00:20:14.080
So we were bait?

00:20:14.970 --> 00:20:18.000
It's because I treated her so badly...

00:20:18.390 --> 00:20:23.840
You did that because the doctor said she should live outside as much as possible.

00:20:23.840 --> 00:20:27.760
She just lost her grandfather. If only I had been kinder to her...

00:20:41.060 --> 00:20:43.070
See you later, Nakasugi-san.

00:20:53.390 --> 00:20:55.250
Baron, what's wrong?

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:58.210
Senkawa-kun?

00:21:01.790 --> 00:21:03.150
Sayaka-ojousan!

00:21:04.570 --> 00:21:06.100
Sayaka-san!

00:21:06.100 --> 00:21:07.440
Sayaka!

00:21:10.740 --> 00:21:12.630
I'm so glad!

00:21:12.630 --> 00:21:13.800
Aunt.

00:21:16.800 --> 00:21:19.020
They seem like good people.

00:21:19.020 --> 00:21:20.860
Yeah, they do.

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:25.730
You sure you're okay with not talking to her?

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:27.800
Yeah, I'm fine.

00:21:33.020 --> 00:21:38.270
Encore!

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:48.250
Goodbye, the one I love.

00:21:58.720 --> 00:22:01.660
Turning your back.

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:04.370
Raising your hand.

00:22:05.160 --> 00:22:10.030
The greeting of parting.

00:22:11.230 --> 00:22:13.770
What kind of expression

00:22:14.180 --> 00:22:16.740
do you have right now?

00:22:16.740 --> 00:22:17.100
I want to know.

00:22:17.100 --> 00:22:18.740
Shion-san.

00:22:18.740 --> 00:22:19.700
I want to know.

00:22:19.700 --> 00:22:22.750
I don't want to know.

00:22:22.750 --> 00:22:25.880
"We are watching."

00:22:25.880 --> 00:22:28.710
That's what you said.

00:22:29.170 --> 00:22:30.280
That's the same as a bond.

00:22:30.280 --> 00:22:31.430
Shion-san.
That's the same as a bond.

00:22:31.430 --> 00:22:34.760
That's the same as a bond.

00:22:34.760 --> 00:22:37.560
I can't fight

00:22:37.560 --> 00:22:40.560
the flowing of time.

00:22:41.210 --> 00:22:44.770
I didn't want to change.

00:22:44.770 --> 00:22:48.360
I believe in love.

00:22:49.150 --> 00:22:52.360
Goodbye, the one I love.

00:22:52.360 --> 00:22:56.620
I'll see you off in the background.

00:22:56.620 --> 00:23:01.720
I realize it now.

00:23:01.720 --> 00:23:04.860
Your smile, your frown.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:08.750
Your kind embrace, your voice.

00:23:08.750 --> 00:23:10.310
Ah.

00:23:10.310 --> 00:23:14.580
It'll always be with you.

00:23:15.730 --> 00:23:18.080
See you.

00:23:18.680 --> 00:23:19.850
Bye bye.

00:23:41.250 --> 00:23:41.990
Good grief.

00:23:41.990 --> 00:23:46.200
That Senkawa... He is always tardy!

00:23:47.030 --> 00:23:48.230
Geez...

00:23:56.290 --> 00:23:57.600
What's wrong?

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:01.310
That looks troubling. Where are you going?

00:24:02.070 --> 00:24:03.300
Want some help?

00:24:04.080 --> 00:24:06.690
Ah, thank you, but...

00:24:08.290 --> 00:24:09.330
Shouko-chan!

00:24:10.300 --> 00:24:11.820
You're late, Nataru!

00:24:12.920 --> 00:24:14.120
I'm sorry, I'm sorry.

00:24:14.120 --> 00:24:16.510
It's my first time buying something like this.

00:24:17.490 --> 00:24:19.220
H-Hello.

00:24:19.220 --> 00:24:22.470
She was worried about me.

00:24:22.470 --> 00:24:24.580
Thank you for your kindness.

00:24:24.580 --> 00:24:26.330
Not at all. I didn't really—

00:24:26.330 --> 00:24:28.460
Wow, they're so cute!

00:24:29.690 --> 00:24:32.290
Yuuichi liked these, after all.

00:24:32.750 --> 00:24:34.170
I'm sure he'll like them.

00:24:34.880 --> 00:24:36.390
Thanks.

00:24:39.590 --> 00:24:42.100
Ah, Senkawa!

00:24:42.390 --> 00:24:44.650
Crap, she's here already!

00:24:45.650 --> 00:24:48.250
Make sure you apologize properly for oversleeping.

00:24:48.250 --> 00:24:49.350
Arrogant...

00:24:49.760 --> 00:24:52.620
Good grief, Senkawa. You know...

00:24:52.620 --> 00:24:54.600
You're always late!

00:24:54.600 --> 00:24:56.440
It's the alien's fault.
Arrive at the time you promise!
